<title>USA: MBIA qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies eight muni issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Corp. said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following eight municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale:</p>
<p>--University of Alaska $10 million general revs.</p>
<p>--San Francisco, Calif., $48.05 million general obligations.</p>
<p>--Maui County, Hawaii, $17.75 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Bannock County SD, Idaho, $27.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Port Huron Area SD, Mich., $7.985 million school building and site bonds.</p>
<p>--Little Egg Harbor Twp., N.J., $2.913 million general improvement.</p>
<p>--New Jersey Educational Facilities $6.77 million revs.</p>
<p>--West Virginia Housing Fund $25 million housing bonds.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
